#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/site-configuration-settings.rst:1588
msgid "Threaded discussions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/site-configuration-settings.rst:1592
msgid ""
"Customers upgrading from a legacy Mattermost release prior to v7.0 must "
"review the `administrator's guide to enabling threaded discussions "
"<https://support.mattermost.com/hc/en-"
"us/articles/6880701948564-Administrator-s-guide-to-enabling-Collapsed-"
"Reply-Threads>`_ (formerly known as Collapsed Reply Threads) prior to "
"enabling this functionality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/site-configuration-settings.rst:1595
msgid ""
"**Always On**: **(Default)** Enables :doc:`threaded discussions </end-"
"user-guide/collaborate/organize-conversations>` on the server and for all"
" users. This is the recommended configuration for optimal user experience"
" and to ensure consistency in how users read and respond to threaded "
"conversations. ``config.json`` setting: ``\"always_on\"``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/site-configuration-settings.rst:1600
msgid ""
"**Default On**: Enables threaded discussions on the server and for all "
"users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/site-configuration-settings.rst:1601
msgid ""
"**Default Off**: Enables threaded discussions on the server but **not** "
"for users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/site-configuration-settings.rst:1602
msgid ""
"**Disabled**: Users cannot enable threaded discussions. ``config.json`` "
"setting: ``\"disabled\"``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/site-configuration-settings.rst:1596
msgid "``config.json`` setting: ``ServiceSettings`` > ``CollapsedThreads``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/site-configuration-settings.rst:1597
msgid "Environment variable: ``MM_SERVICESETTINGS_COLLAPSEDTHREADS``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/site-configuration-settings.rst:1616
msgid "Message priority"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/site-configuration-settings.rst:1619
msgid ""
"`Mattermost Enterprise or Professional "
"<https://mattermost.com/pricing>`__ customers can additionally request "
"message acknowledgements to track that specific, time-sensitive messages "
"have been seen and actioned. See the :doc:`message priority </end-user-"
"guide/collaborate/message-priority>` documentation to learn more."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/site-configuration-settings.rst:1623
msgid ""
"**true**: **(Default)** Enables message priority for all users which "
"enables them to set a visual indiciator for important or urgent root "
"messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/site-configuration-settings.rst:1626
msgid ""
"**false**: Disables the ability to set message priority and request "
"acknowledgements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/site-configuration-settings.rst:1624
msgid "``config.json`` setting: ``ServiceSettings`` > ``PostPriority`` > ``true``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/site-configuration-settings.rst:1625
msgid "Environment variable: ``MM_SERVICESETTINGS_POSTPRIORITY``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/site-configuration-settings.rst:1632
msgid ""
"Disabling this configuration setting in larger deployments may improve "
"server performance in the following areas, particularly in environments "
"where performance and responsiveness are critical:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/site-configuration-settings.rst:1634
msgid ""
"Simplified Processing: When post priority is enabled, the system has to "
"manage and prioritize posts based on their designated priority levels. "
"This adds additional processing overhead as the system must evaluate and "
"sort posts accordingly. By disabling this feature, all posts are treated "
"equally, which simplifies the processing logic and reduces the "
"computational load."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/site-configuration-settings.rst:1635
msgid ""
"Reduced Latency: With post priority enabled, there might be delays "
"introduced while the system determines the priority of each post and "
"processes them in the correct order. Disabling post priority can lead to "
"more consistent and potentially quicker handling of posts because the "
"system processes them on a first-come, first-served basis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/site-configuration-settings.rst:1636
msgid ""
"Lower Resource Utilization: Managing post priorities can consume "
"additional system resources such as CPU and memory. Disabling this "
"feature can free up these resources, allowing the system to allocate them"
" to other tasks, thereby improving overall performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/site-configuration-settings.rst:1637
msgid ""
"Improved Scalability: In a high-traffic environment, the complexity of "
"managing post priorities can become more pronounced. Disabling this "
"feature simplifies the system's operations, making it easier to scale as "
"the number of users and posts increases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/configure/site-configuration-settings.rst:1650
msgid "Persistent notifications"
msgstr ""

